menu "mbedTLS"

    config MBEDTLS_USE_BUNDLED_PQC
        bool "Use bundled hybrid-PQC mbedTLS (instead of default ESP-IDF mbedTLS)"
        default y
        help
            esp-pqc ships an override of ESP-IDF's builtin mbedTLS component
            (components/mbedtls, wired up via override_path in
            idf_component.yml). This option chooses which mbedTLS source tree
            that override builds; components/mbedtls/CMakeLists.txt reads it.

            y - Build the bundled hybrid-PQC mbedTLS submodule shipped in this
                component (components/mbedtls/mbedtls). This tree adds the TLS 1.3
                hybrid post-quantum additions (X25519MLKEM768 key exchange and
                ML-DSA-65 authentication) used by the esp_hybrid_tls example. The
                actual PQC features are still gated by the "Hybrid PQC TLS" options
                below (esp-pqc injects the liboqs include path and feature macros
                onto the mbedTLS targets at configure time).

            n - Build the default ESP-IDF mbedTLS (the overridden $IDF_PATH tree),
                exactly as if this override component were not present. Use this for
                projects that do not need the PQC/hybrid-TLS additions.

            Default is y so the bundled PQC mbedTLS is used whenever this component
            is in the build. Set to n in sdkconfig.defaults for non-PQC projects.

    menu "Hybrid PQC TLS"
        depends on LIBOQS_ENABLED && MBEDTLS_USE_BUNDLED_PQC

        config MBEDTLS_SSL_TLS1_3_KEY_EXCHANGE_GROUP_X25519MLKEM768
            bool "Enable X25519MLKEM768 hybrid KEM group (TLS 1.3)"
            depends on LIBOQS_ENABLE_KEM_ML_KEM
            default y
            help
                Enables TLS 1.3 hybrid key exchange using X25519 + ML-KEM-768
                (IANA group codepoint 0x11EC).

                Also requires TLS 1.3 in mbedTLS
                (CONFIG_MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_TLS1_3), a main task stack of at least
                16 KB, and a partition table with at least a 2 MB app partition.
                The server must support X25519MLKEM768 (e.g. OpenSSL 3.5+ with
                -groups X25519MLKEM768).

                When set, esp-pqc injects the liboqs include path and defines
                the MBEDTLS_SSL_TLS1_3_KEY_EXCHANGE_GROUP_X25519MLKEM768 macro on
                the mbedTLS library targets at configure time, so ESP-IDF's
                mbedtls component itself needs no patching. The application MUST
                list 'mbedtls' before 'esp-pqc' in its REQUIRES so the mbedTLS
                targets exist when esp-pqc wires them.

        config MBEDTLS_SSL_TLS1_3_SIG_MLDSA65
            bool "Enable ML-DSA-65 (pure) TLS 1.3 and X.509 verification"
            depends on LIBOQS_ENABLE_SIG_ML_DSA
            default y
            help
                TLS SignatureScheme 0x0905 and X.509 id-ml-dsa-65 (RFC 9881).

                When set, esp-pqc defines MBEDTLS_SSL_TLS1_3_SIG_MLDSA65 for
                the mbedTLS build.

    endmenu

endmenu
